SLTriggers Redux - Licensing

SUMMARY
-------
- Source code, scripts, and other files in this repository: MIT License (see
  the sections below).
- The compiled SKSE plugin (sl-triggers.dll) statically links CommonLibSSE-NG
  and is therefore distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3
  or (at your option) any later version (GPL-3.0-or-later). See the next
  section.

================================================================================
COMPILED SKSE PLUGIN - GPL-3.0-or-later (CommonLibSSE-NG)
================================================================================

The SKSE plugin (sl-triggers.dll) is built against CommonLibSSE-NG
(https://github.com/alandtse/CommonLibSSE-NG), which is licensed under
GPL-3.0-or-later with a Modding Exception and a GPL-3.0 Linking Exception
(see EXCEPTIONS.md in that project). The Modding Exception covers linking with
Skyrim itself and with SKSE and Windows. It does not extend to plugin code, so
a plugin that statically links CommonLibSSE-NG forms a combined work with it.

Accordingly, the compiled plugin binary is conveyed under the terms of the GNU
General Public License, version 3 or later:

    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

The complete corresponding source code for the plugin, including the portions
that are otherwise MIT licensed, is available at:

    https://github.com/sltriggersredux/sltriggersredux

This applies only to the compiled plugin binary. The MIT-licensed source files
in this repository remain available under the MIT License below, and you may
use them under those terms in works that do not link CommonLibSSE-NG. Papyrus
scripts, SLT scripts, configuration, FOMOD files, and documentation are
separate works that do not link CommonLibSSE-NG and remain under the MIT
License.

CommonLibSSE-NG is Copyright (c) its respective authors and contributors, and
was originally based on code released under the MIT License
(CommonLibSSE, (c) Ryan-rsm-McKenzie). Its license texts (COPYING.txt and
EXCEPTIONS.md) accompany distributions of the plugin binary.

This project contains code from multiple sources with different licensing:

